# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command memfind
usage 1   memfind <space> <bytes> [<max>]  find every offset where <bytes> occurs (hex pairs, '??' matches
usage 2                                 any byte, separators optional) - default at most 20 hits

case byte patterns
target fake
covers 1-2
$ memfind
out 38
Usage: memfind <space> <bytes> [<max>]
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM
out 38
Usage: memfind <space> <bytes> [<max>]
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 03
out 48
1 match(es) for the 1-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 030A
out 48
1 match(es) for the 2-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM '03 ?? 11'
out 92
Pattern must be whole hex byte pairs, using '??' for a wildcard - e.g. 00FF11 or '00 ?? 11'.
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 03-0A-11
out 48
1 match(es) for the 3-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 0 
out 92
Pattern must be whole hex byte pairs, using '??' for a wildcard - e.g. 00FF11 or '00 ?? 11'.
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 0
out 92
Pattern must be whole hex byte pairs, using '??' for a wildcard - e.g. 00FF11 or '00 ?? 11'.
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM zz
out 92
Pattern must be whole hex byte pairs, using '??' for a wildcard - e.g. 00FF11 or '00 ?? 11'.
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM ??
out 177
More than 20 match(es) in RAM - showing the first 20:
  0x0
  0x1
  0x2
  0x3
  0x4
  0x5
  0x6
  0x7
  0x8
  0x9
  0xA
  0xB
  0xC
  0xD
  0xE
  0xF
  0x10
  0x11
  0x12
  0x13
status 0
action none
$ memfind IO F0
out 143
IO can have real side effects on read (live hardware registers) - refusing a bulk scan there. Try WRAM (or another plain-memory space) instead.
status 0
action none
$ memfind ROM EA 3
out 69
More than 3 match(es) in ROM - showing the first 3:
  0xC
  0xD
  0xE
status 0
action none
$ memfind ROM EA EA 2
out 63
More than 2 match(es) in ROM - showing the first 2:
  0xC
  0xD
status 0
action none
$ memfind NOPE 00
out 83
Error: No memory space named 'NOPE'. Available: RAM, ROM, VRAM, IO, UNSIZED, CpuBus
status 1
action none
$ memfind RAM FFFF
out 35
No match for 2-byte pattern in RAM.
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ memfind RAM 00
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
end

case a trailing pair of decimal digits is read as the limit
target fake
covers 1-2
$ memfind RAM 03 0A 11
out 48
1 match(es) for the 2-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 030A11
out 48
1 match(es) for the 3-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
$ memfind RAM 03 0A 11 5
out 48
1 match(es) for the 3-byte pattern in RAM:
  0x0
status 0
action none
end
